==English==
{{was wotd|2023|December|10}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|upér}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*-nós|*-teh₂ts}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|sovereynte}}, {{m|enm|souvereynte}}{{nb...|soueraynete, soueraynte, souereynte, sovereinete, soverente, sufferaigntie, suffranti, suffrauntè, suffreinte|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|sovereyneté}}, {{m|xno|soverentee}}, and {{der|en|fro|souveraineté}} (modern {{cog|fr|souvraineté}}),<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=6770366635|date=July 2023}}</ref> from {{m|fro|soverain}} + {{m|fro|-té|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|noun}}s, often denoting a property or quality}}. {{m|fro||Soverain}} is derived from {{der|en|VL.|*superānus|t=chief; sovereign}}, from {{der|en|la|super|t=above; on top of}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*upér|t=above, over}}) + {{m|la|-ānus|t=suffix meaning ‘of or pertaining to’, usually denoting a relationship of origin, position, or possession}}). The English word is analysable as {{suffix|en|sovereign|ty|pos2=suffix forming {{glossary|abstract noun}}s from {{glossary|adjective}}s}}.

