===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|uncountable}} The [[quality#Noun|quality]] or [[state#Noun|state]] of being [[sovereign#Adjective|sovereign]].
## Of a [[ruler]] (especially a [[monarch]]): [[supreme#Adjective|supreme]] [[authority]] or [[dominion]] over all [[thing]]s.
##* {{RQ:Spenser Shepheardes Calender|chapter=April|gloss=1|folio=15|verso=1|passage={{...}} {{w|Zephyrus}} the VVeſterne vvind being in loue vvith her &#91;[[w:Chloris (nymph)|Chloris]]&#93;, and coueting her to vvyfe, gaue her for a dovvrie, the chiefedome and '''ſoueraigntye''' of al flovvers and greene herbes, grovving on earth.}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare King John|act=II|scene=ii|page=8|column=2|passage=But Fortune, oh, / She is corrupted, chang'd, and vvonne from thee, / Sh'adulterates hourely vvith thine Vnckle ''[[w:John, King of England|Iohn]]'', / And vvith her golden hand hath pluckt on France / To tread dovvne faire reſpect of '''Soueraigntie''', / And made his Maieſtie the bavvd to theirs.}}
## {{lb|en|by extension}} Of a [[nation]] or other [[polity]]: the [[state#Noun|state]] of being able to [[control#Verb|control]] [[resource#Noun|resources]] and [[make#Verb|make]] [[law#Noun|laws]] [[independently]], without the [[coercion]] or [[concurrence]] of other polities.
##: {{synonyms|en|autarchy|independence|nationality|nationhood}}
##: {{coordinate terms|en|autonomy|semiautonomy}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Anouar Abdel-Malek|chapter=Sociology of National Development: Problems of Conceptualisation|title=Nation and Revolution|series=Social Dialectics|seriesvolume=2|location=Albany, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:SUNY Press|State University of New York Press]]|year=1981|section=part I (The Nation as Crucible)|page=13|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/socialdialectics0000abde/page/13/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-87395-501-0|passage=On the other hand, the nationalitarian phenomenon is one in which 'the struggle against the imperialist powers of occupation has as its object, beyond the clearing of the national territory, the independence and '''sovereignty''' of the national State, uprooting in depth the positions of the ex-colonial power&nbsp;– the reconquest of the power of decision in all domains of national life, the prelude to that reconquest of identity  which is at the heart of the renaissance undertaken on the basis of fundamental national demands, and ceaselessly contested, by every means available, on every level, and notably on the internal level'.}}
##* {{RQ:Guardian|author=w:Manuel Valls|title=What have Britain and Catalonia got in common? Delusions of independence|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230929153012/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/mar/07/brexit-catalonia-brexit-independence-leads-to-loss-of-sovereignty|date=7 March 2019|passage=In today's interconnected economies and societies, a formal independence is the opposite of gaining real '''sovereignty''' and control. This is because the excluded party would be absent from the table when decisions are made, unable to participate as choices are taken that, sooner or later, will affect them.}}
## {{lb|en|by extension}} Of a [[person#Noun|person]]: the [[liberty]] to [[decide]] one's [[action#Noun|actions]] and [[thought#Noun|thoughts]].
## [[preeminent|Pre-eminent]] or [[superior#Adjective|superior]] [[excellence]]; also, superior [[ability]] to [[achieve]] something; [[mastery]].
##* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=i|sig=B2|page=29|passage=[His head,] Wherein by curious '''ſoueraigntie''' of Art, / Are fixt his piercing inſtruments of ſight: / Whose fiery circles beare encompaſſed / A heauen of heauenly bodies in their Spheares: {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Love's Labour's Lost Q1|act=IV|scene=iii|sig=F|verso=1|lines=234–237|page=41|passage=Of all complexions the culd '''ſoueraigntie''', / Do meete as at a faire in her faire cheeke, / VVhere ſeuerall vvorthies make one dignitie, / VVhere nothing vvantes, that vvant itſelfe doth ſeeke.}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare All's Well|act=I|scene=iii|page=234|column=2|passage=You knovv my Father left me ſome preſcriptions / Of rare and prou'd effects, ſuch as his reading / And manifeſt experience, had collected / For generall '''ſoueraigntie''': and that he vvil'd me / In heedfull'ſt reſeruation to beſtovv them, / As notes, vvhose faculties incluſiue vvere, / More then they vvere in note: {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Guillim Heraldrie|chapter=Sect[ion] II. Chap[ter] III.|page=43|passage=[Ordinaries in heraldry] are alſo called, ''moſt vvorthy partitions'', in reſpect that albeit the ''Field'' be ''charged'' in diuers parts thereof, vvhether vvith things of one or of diuers kindes, yet is euery of them as effectuall as if it vvere onely one, by the '''Soueraigntie''' of theſe ''partitions'' being interpoſed betvveene them.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[territory]] under the [[rule#Noun|rule]] of a [[sovereign]]; an [[independent#Adjective|independent]] or [[self-governing]] nation or other polity.

